CORE
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ deduced type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The second use of vb<char> instantiates the specialization again; the new
declaration still has the placeholder type, and was rejected ("symbol
'vb<char>' already declared with different type: original: signed int,
new: auto", combine_types).  combine_types now keeps the deduced type,
and the repeated initializer is dropped, since it would replace the
converted value of the first instantiation.  N5008 [temp.spec.general]/5.
